    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0137" n="971" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg971"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.96/332</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-09T11:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.17 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1124. For War Trade Board:</p>
                <p>Does vessel from Spain to America via Panama Canal, not stopping at Canal ports,
                    have to subject itself to jurisdiction of Board? If so, what must owners do?
                    Please instruct. Chadbourne.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
